## Controlling VPS replacement

Changes to `user_data` or `user_data_format` replace the VPS because inline
user data is applied only when the VPS is created.

### Ignore inline user-data changes

To keep the existing VPS while applying other configuration changes, add both
arguments to `ignore_changes`:

```terraform
lifecycle {
  ignore_changes = [
    user_data,
    user_data_format,
  ]
}
```

Changes to these arguments are then ignored. The new user data is not applied
to the existing VPS.

### Block replacement and destruction

To reject a plan that would replace or destroy the VPS while it remains in the
configuration, enable `prevent_destroy`:

```terraform
lifecycle {
  prevent_destroy = true
}
```

`prevent_destroy` does not ignore user-data changes. A user-data change still
requires VPS replacement, but the plan or apply fails because replacement would
destroy the existing VPS. Revert the change or remove the guard before
replacement can proceed.

